<Base title="Privacy | The Crypto Realm" description="How The Crypto Realm handles visitor information.">
  <section class="container page-title">
    <div class="eyebrow">LEGAL</div>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="subtle">Last updated: November 13, 2026</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="article-body">
      <p>This page explains, in plain language, what happens to your information when you visit The Crypto Realm.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>You don’t need an account to use this site, and we don’t ask you to fill in forms. Apart from the advertising and embedded content described below, the site itself doesn’t set cookies.</p>
      <p>We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see which pages are read and which links are clicked. According to Cloudflare, it is built to be privacy-focused: it counts visits without using cookies and without tracking individuals across websites. Cloudflare also hosts this site, and like any web host it processes visitors’ IP addresses to deliver pages and protect against attacks.</p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>This site may show ads served by Google AdSense. Google and its partners use cookies and similar technology to show ads based on your visits to this and other websites. In some regions, such as the EU and UK, you may see a consent message before ads are shown.</p>
      <p>You can manage or turn off personalized ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s Ads Settings</a>, or opt out of many third-party advertising cookies at <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>. To learn how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s explanation</a>.</p>

      <h2>Embedded videos and images</h2>
      <p>Some pages embed YouTube videos using YouTube’s privacy-enhanced mode, and the “Latest videos” thumbnails load from YouTube’s servers. When a video loads or plays, YouTube (Google) may receive information such as your IP address and may set its own cookies. Their privacy policy applies to that data.</p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>This site links to services such as YouTube, Rumble, Facebook, Instagram, RedBubble, Amazon, crypto exchanges, NFT marketplaces and a hardware wallet seller. Those sites have their own privacy policies. Some of our links are referral or affiliate links, which means the other site may use a cookie to record that you came from us so a reward can be credited. See our <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> for details.</p>

      <h2>If you email us</h2>
      <p>If you write to <a href="mailto:thecryptorealm@outlook.com">thecryptorealm@outlook.com</a>, we use your email address and message only to reply to you. We don’t sell or share them.</p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>You can block cookies and trackers in your browser settings, and the site will still work. To ask about an email you’ve sent us, or to have it deleted, write to the address above.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change how the site works, we’ll update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
